--- A column the program reads as a position holds ints, and only such a
--- use asks the file for ints: a file with 1.5 there stops the load with
--- the column, what it holds, what the program reads and the read that
--- asked — the same words in both modes, before any cell is read. (A
--- column only compared with an int is a number, floats or ints as the
--- file has them: parity 192.)
use frame

write['parity_196.csv', 'name,slot\na,0\nb,1.5\n']

labels = ['first', 'second']
df = frame.load['parity_196.csv']
rm['parity_196.csv']
for i in df.slot
    log[labels[i]]
